{# Fil d'Ariane — visible only when the site runs as an installed PWA
   (display-mode: standalone). Visibility is 100% CSS (see app.css's
   .breadcrumb-bar rule) — no server flag, no JS detection, since this is a
   navigation convenience, never a security boundary (SECURITY §3, same
   principle as menu visibility).

   The home icon is always hard-coded to "/", never sourced from config.
   Everything past it comes from the current route's optional `breadcrumb`
   declaration (Core\Http\Router::addRoute()'s 6th argument for core routes,
   module.json's `routes[].breadcrumb` for module routes) — a route that
   declares none simply stops the trail at the home icon. `parents` are
   ancestor labels naming a *menu* (Core\View\MenuBuilder's `label`, e.g.
   "Espace des chefs") — most menu categories still have no single landing
   page of their own (never invent one, e.g. writing "/" or "#"), so a
   parent is a clickable link only when the matching menu in `menus`
   actually has a real, non-dynamic, non-separator first page to send
   people to, other than the page already being viewed (linking a parent
   back to itself — e.g. "Espace des chefs" on /chefs/staffs, currently
   that menu's only static page — would be a dead click); otherwise it
   stays plain text, exactly as before. This is a template-side lookup
   against the same `menus` global the nav already renders from — no new
   data on the breadcrumb declaration itself.
   `breadcrumb_current`, when the controller passes it, replaces the
   route's static `label` for a dynamic page title (a member's name, an
   article title...); the current page is never itself a link. #}
<nav class="breadcrumb-bar border-bottom bg-light px-3 py-2" aria-label="Fil d'Ariane">
    <ol class="breadcrumb mb-0 small align-items-center">
        <li class="breadcrumb-item">
            <a href="/" class="text-decoration-none" aria-label="Accueil">
                <i class="bi bi-house-door"></i>
            </a>
        </li>
        {% set breadcrumb = route_breadcrumb|default(null) %}
        {% if breadcrumb is not null and current_path|default('/') != '/' %}
            {% for parent in breadcrumb.parents %}
                {% set parent_url = null %}
                {% for menu in menus|default([]) %}
                    {% if menu.label == parent %}
                        {% for page in menu.pages %}
                            {% if parent_url is null and not page.isSeparator and not page.isDynamic and page.url is defined and page.url != '' and page.url != '#' and page.url != current_path|default('/') %}
                                {% set parent_url = page.url %}
                            {% endif %}
                        {% endfor %}
                    {% endif %}
                {% endfor %}
                {% if parent_url is not null %}
                    <li class="breadcrumb-item"><a href="{{ parent_url }}" class="text-decoration-none">{{ parent }}</a></li>
                {% else %}
                    <li class="breadcrumb-item text-body-secondary">{{ parent }}</li>
                {% endif %}
            {% endfor %}
            <li class="breadcrumb-item active text-truncate" aria-current="page">
                {{ breadcrumb_current|default(breadcrumb.label) }}
            </li>
        {% endif %}
    </ol>
</nav>
